            <!-- Section 1: Studio & Scoped Architecture -->
            <section class="content-section" id="app-architecture">
                <h2>Studio IDE &amp; Scoped Application Architecture</h2>
                <p>
                    In modern ServiceNow development, enterprise solutions are built as <strong>Scoped Applications</strong> rather than 
                    modifying the global namespace. Scopes create a cryptographic and logical sandbox that encapsulates all application 
                    artifacts—tables, client scripts, business rules, flows, and ACLs.
                </p>

                <div class="feature-grid">
                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Namespace Isolation</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Every custom artifact is prefixed with the unique company scope identifier (e.g. <code>x_acme_equip_pass</code>). 
                            This guarantees that custom field names will never collide with ServiceNow core platform upgrades or store plugins.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Git Source Control Integration</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Studio connects directly to GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket over SSH/HTTPS. Developers commit changes, branch features, 
                            and resolve pull requests using standard Git workflows rather than manual update set stitching.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-card">
                        <div class="feature-card-header">
                            <h4>Access Containment</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Cross-scope security prevents rogue scripts from other applications from querying, altering, or deleting your data 
                            unless explicitly granted via <strong>Restricted Caller Access (RCA)</strong> or Cross-Scope Privileges.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="diagram-block">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Scoped Application Containment Architecture</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    graph TD
                        subgraph GlobalScope["Global Scope (Core Platform)"]
                            TaskTable["Task Base Table (task)"]
                            UserTable["User Table (sys_user)"]
                            AssetTable["Hardware Assets (alm_hardware)"]
                        end

                        subgraph CustomAppScope["Scoped App Sandbox (x_acme_equip_pass)"]
                            CustomTable["Equipment Pass Table (x_acme_equip_pass)"]
                            AppUIPolicy["Client Validation &amp; UI Policies"]
                            AppBR["Server Business Rules &amp; Flows"]
                            AppRoles["App Roles (admin, user)"]
                        end

                        CustomTable -->|Extends parent task| TaskTable
                        CustomTable -->|References borrower| UserTable
                        CustomTable -->|References asset tag| AssetTable

                        AppUIPolicy -.->|Controls Form UI| CustomTable
                        AppBR -.->|Database Interceptor| CustomTable
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

